Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRule", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"b370a163-aba2-b943-b0a9-fb8989245e9f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "[", 
    RowBox[{"input", ",", " ", "output"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"ee146900-47c1-494b-9ca4-82edda7af5c1"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewrite rule taking the hypergraph input to the hypergraph \
output."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"55675b70-a720-2f4d-b1ff-3bfa1aa8fdc0"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"ac891364-a5de-ea4f-9535-02dd7676a660"],

Cell["\<\
Either side may be given as anything Hypergraph accepts, and is converted; a \
side that is not a hypergraph gives HypergraphRule::hg.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"952f41b5-0abe-1644-b9e2-95697e99a81a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8d441136-a474-5948-b0d2-fcd57e81e4a9"],
 " applies the rule, giving one event for every way the input matches. See ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"09f154d5-4b17-8641-995e-db34f75df231"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c4fe0921-a2d7-8140-ad73-25575d877751"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex of the input that the output keeps is carried through the rewrite; \
one the output introduces is created fresh; one the output drops is \
destroyed. \"SharedVertices\", \"NewVertices\" and \"DeletedVertices\" report \
the three groups, read off the two sides by vertex identifier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d61849e7-e7f2-194a-a7b7-8abfeb77c4b7"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices correspond between the two sides by identifier, so the same name on \
both sides means the same vertex, and a name on the output alone means a new \
one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a53672ee-8474-5c4d-8208-c31e6f83e7ee"],

Cell["\<\
The shape follows the reference paclet this package grew out of, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fe7b0bb4-f961-8c44-80db-d1aad57ef80f"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"abf9979b-a26c-c242-9e41-ae7d287adaf4"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge: the two endpoints are kept, a third vertex is new.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"cc388bcb-2e43-f14b-9e71-5521880ca51a"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f925069d-f5c5-244e-aeca-05a1b301781d"],

